  "id": "central-coherence-theory",
  "term": "central coherence theory",
  "definition": "Central coherence theory is a cognitive account used to explain some features of autism. In its weak form, it proposes that autistic individuals tend to process details more strongly than the overall whole or “big picture,” which can affect tasks that rely on integrating information.",
